e {\n    Execute(ctx context.Context, task Task) (Result, error)\n}\n```\n\n## 配置污染防护（测试）\n\n全局 `~/.rick/config.json` 的 `max_retries` 高值会导致测试超时（retry sleep 累计）。测试开头注入临时 HOME：\n\n```go\nfunc TestXxx(t *testing.T) {\n    dir := t.TempDir()\n    t.Setenv(\"HOME\", dir)\n    _ = os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(dir, \".rick\"), 0755)\n    _ = os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, \".rick\", \"config.json\"),\n        []byte(`{\"max_retries\":2}`), 0644)\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n识别信号：本地测试卡 > 30s，stack trace 卡在 `retry.go time.Sleep`，CI 正常。\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786900483577}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding. Let me also check the commands.md and go-patterns.md quickly for interface contract facts (runtime Run signature etc.). Actually, the task description already gives me the exact content I need to write. Let me check commands.md for a bit more detail on command behaviors and dry-run, and go-patterns.md for DIP.\n\nActually, I think I have enough. The key facts for the rick-spec.md are:\n\n1. Four-layer architecture (calling top-down):\n   - Layer 1 (entry): CLI / TUI / WEB-UI (route commands, parse args, interactive presentation)\n   - Layer 2 (dispatch/aggregation): handler (accept entry params, orchestrate env/runtime/builder)\n   - Layer 3 (execution): env (pi/dsh & extensions check/install/config/maintenance) + runtime (pi/dsh call wrapper: param parse + call) + builder (assemble pi/dsh prompt artifacts per entry)\n   - Layer 4 (infrastructure): pi (current runtime) / dsh (reserved runtime) / workspace (path resolution) / config (~/.rick/config.json loading)\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Exception 1: env ↔ dsh mutual call (dsh ecosystem interaction, not pure one-way; do NOT list dshRuntime/dshBuilder nodes separately; links directly to components env and dsh)\n     - Exception 2: TUI / WEB-UI cross-layer direct connection to pi/dsh (interactive UI directly drives runtime, bypassing handler/env/runtime/builder)\n     - Exception 3: composition root (cmd RunE lazy instantiate piRuntime/piEnv/pibuilder inject into handler) is DIP composition root pattern, cross-layer exemption\n     - Exception 4: workspace/config are cross-layer leaf infrastructure (path resolution/config loading), can be directly used by any layer, not participating in functional call chain \"level-by-level down\" constraint\n\n2. 5 modules responsibilities and boundaries (env four responsibilities, runtime responsibilities, handler responsibilities, builder three things); internal/prompt = L3 templates carrier package; L3 internal (env/runtime/builder) can reuse shared path tools (AgentDir/RuntimeDir/RuntimeBin/AgentEnv etc.), not considered cross-layer callback\n\n3. builder three things contract (templates = go embed embedded prompts; pibuilder = pi unified entry compositor builder; xxxxbuilder = extension slot)\n\n4. runtime contract: launch pi + internal check session ready + return (sessionID, behavior trace)\n\n5. Deletion list: executor (dispatch→pi), parser (read/validate→pi), actpath (trace→runtime), logging (dead code), git (→pi script), agent interface (lost consumer)\n\n6. Acceptance criteria: functional equivalence = pass all functional acceptance; rick made thin (dag dispatch and gates sunk to pi); single runtime (pi) as current implementation - reserve three extension seams for future deepseek harness(dsh): builder's RuntimeBuilder (= xxxxbuilder escape layer), runtime's Runtime (Name/Run), env's RuntimeEnv (Ensure/DeployCustomizations/CheckReady) + config runtime field (default pi); current pi is only implementation, don't write dsh code\n\n7. Key results detail:\n   - KR2: env four responsibilities\n   - KR3: runtime responsibilities + handler responsibilities + injection model (method(system prompt) + skills + instance(user prompt) three-layer separation - method via --append-system-prompt (keep pi default skeleton), skills via pi skills mechanism, instance via prompt file)\n   - KR4: sink strategy: dag scheduling → pi workflowScript orchestration (await sequence), gates → pi hook (rick-gates extension) + deterministic scripts; think/research/exporter → pi agent (env responsibility 3 deployment)\n   - KR5: extension seams: RuntimeBuilder, Runtime, RuntimeEnv + config runtime field (default pi); \"adding dsh only adds dshBuilder/dshRuntime/dshEnv three implementations and registers, cli/handler/method layer templates unchanged\"\n   - KR6: four-layer architecture diagram (mermaid/text): layer1 CLI/TUI/WEB-UI → layer2 handl