{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The doing_check requires:\n1. tasks.json exists and parseable\n2. debug/ dir: no bug*.md files with wrong format (no debug/ is fine)\n3. No tasks in \"running\" zombie state\n4. All success tasks have non-empty commit_hash\n\nCurrently task2 status is \"running\" in tasks.json. So if I run doing_check now, it will fail because task2 is \"running\". But wait — the doing_check is run by the Sub Agent at COMMIT step. Actually, the flow is: I'm the Main Agent (or am I the Sub Agent?).\n\nActually the prompt says I need to do the Doing Loop myself. The key thing: I need to mark task2 success with a commit_hash. This is the mark-task-success flow.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The task status in tasks.json is \"running\" for task2. The doing_check will fail if a task is \"running\" (zombie). So to make doing_check pass, I need to:\n1. Complete the work (write rick-spec.md, commit it with a commit hash)\n2. Update tasks.json: mark task2 status=\"success\" and set commit_hash to the commit hash.\n\nBut wait — how does the normal doing flow mark task success? The runner marks tasks success. Let me look at how tasks.json gets updated. There's a `mark-task-success` skill and `do-check-mark-success-loop`. \n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole flow. The prompt's \"第二步：格式检查\" says run `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/bin/rick tools doing_check job_35` and check pass.\n\nFor doing_check to pass, task2 (and task1) must not be \"running\", and success tasks must have commit_hash. task1 is already success with commit_hash. task2 is \"running\" currently.\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Commit the rick-spec.md (and maybe README index update).\n2. Update tasks.json to mark task2 as \"success\" with the new commit hash.\n\nLet me look at how the mark-task-success skill / doing flow updates tasks.json. Let me check the tasks_json.go and how runner marks success.\n\nActually, let me check the mark