ntracked files (project-conventions.md, dream_prompt.md, etc.) that are NOT part of my task. I must be careful to only `git add` the files relevant to task2: `.rick/domain/rick-spec.md`, and optionally `.rick/domain/README.md`.\n\nBut wait — there are already modified files in the working tree from other tasks/jobs. The mark_task_success.py will update tasks.json, which is already modified (it's in \"modified\" list). Actually tasks.json is already modified in git status (\"modified: .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json\"). That's because task1 already updated it (status running for task2, and task1 success). Hmm wait, actually the task1 commit d3cbb3d \"chore(task1): mark task1 success in tasks.json\" — that commit should have already committed tasks.json with task1 success and task2 running. Let me check current git diff of tasks.json.\n\nActually git status shows \"modified: .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json\" still. That's odd if task1 already committed it. Let me check git log for tasks.json and current diff.\n\nActually, let me look more carefully. The current tasks.json on disk (which I read earlier) shows task1 success (commit d3cbb3d...), task2 running. But git status shows tasks.json as modified. This means the committed version differs from disk. Let me check `git diff .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json`.\n\nLet me investigate the git state carefully before committing."}}
