ns and registers, cli/handler/method layer templates unchanged\"\n   - KR6: four-layer architecture diagram (mermaid/text): layer1 CLI/TUI/WEB-UI → layer2 handler → layer3 env/runtime/builder → layer4 pi/dsh/workspace/config; mark \"level-by-level down\" + exception1 \"env ↔ dsh mutual call (don't single-list dshRuntime/dshBuilder nodes)\" + exception2 \"TUI/WEB-UI cross-layer direct to pi/dsh\"\n\nThe test script checks for these keywords:\n- Module names: cli, handler, env, builder, runtime (note: case sensitive, must be lowercase! \"CLI\" for the layer but \"cli\" for module name)\n- env four responsibilities: 安装, 生态扩展, 定制, 就绪\n- 4-layer keywords: 第一层, 第二层, 第三层, 第四层, CLI, TUI, WEB-UI\n- RFC keywords: dag, 门禁, sessionID\n- extension seams: RuntimeBuilder, RuntimeEnv, runtime (note: \"runtime\" lowercase, also \"RuntimeBuilder\" and \"RuntimeEnv\" exact case)\n- '{{' must be 0\n\nNote: the keyword \"runtime\" must appear lowercase. \"Runtime\" (capital R) is different from \"runtime\" — but \"RuntimeBuilder\" contains \"Runtime\" not \"runtime\". \"RuntimeEnv\" contains \"Runtime\" not \"runtime\". So I need a lowercase \"runtime\" somewhere. It will appear naturally.\n\nAlso \"cli\" must appear lowercase. \"CLI\" is uppercase but \"cli\" appears in \"cli 命令\" etc. I'll make sure both.\n\nNow, one concern: The spec.md template says four elements must each be independent sections (模块边界 / 职责 / 接口契约 / 验收标准). I need to structure rick-spec.md accordingly.\n\nLet me also confirm no `{{` anywhere — I should not use template-style placeholders. Also no `<...>` placeholders left unreplaced? The spec.md says placeholders use `<...>` and must be replaced. But the test only checks `{{`. However, to follow the spec norm, I should avoid leaving `<...>` placeholders. I'll write concrete content.\n\nNow let me think about the \"四要素结构\" (four-element structure) requirement: 模块边界 (module boundaries) / 职责 (responsibilities) / 接口契约 (interface contracts) / 验收标准 (acceptance criteria). I